# A pattern detector's own tests, fixtures, and docs necessarily contain the
# patterns it detects (`: any`, `pickle.loads(`, `print(`, …) as test data or
# documentation. Exclude them so `guideline-checker check` passes on this repo.
tests
README.md
DECISIONS.md
CHANGELOG.md

# Pattern-definition modules: a substring detector's own detector tables, its
# LLM prompt examples, and its scaffold templates necessarily contain the very
# patterns they flag (`eval(`, `exec(`, `shell=True`, `os.system(`, …). Those
# matches are the engine's data, not violations of it. The rest of the library
# (loader, guidelines, persist, sandbox, web, scanners, …) stays checked.
guideline_checker/proposer.py
guideline_checker/init_cmd.py
scripts

# checker.py and cli.py are NOT excluded here (D-0021): a file-level blanket also
# blinds the numeric measurement rules (py-file-length, py-function-length) to
# the two longest files in the repo. The pattern rules that legitimately match
# them carry a per-rule `detect.exclude` instead — `py-no-eval-exec` excludes
# checker.py (its detector tables hold `eval(`/`exec(`), `py-structured-logging`
# excludes cli.py (a CLI's stdout IS its interface, so `print(` is correct).
